## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical RN skills: list rendering, FlatList optimization, local filtering, and simple interactivity with pull-to-refresh. It checks understanding of render perf basics for beginner level in a real app.

## Key Concepts

- FlatList basics and keyExtractor
- React.memo for item rows
- useMemo for derived data
- Debounced search input
- Pull-to-refresh with refreshControl

## Code Example

```javascript
import React, {useState, useMemo, useCallback} from 'react';
import {FlatList, TextInput, View, Text, RefreshControl} from 'react-native';

const ContactRow = React.memo(({c}) => (
  <View style={{padding:8}}>
    <Text>{c.firstName} {c.lastName}</Text>
    <Text>{c.phone}</Text>
  </View>
));

export default function Contacts({data}) {
  const [q, setQ] = useState('');
  const [refreshing, setRefreshing] = useState(false);

  const filtered = useMemo(() => data.filter(c => {
    const n = (c.firstName + ' ' + c.lastName).toLowerCase();
    return n.includes(q.toLowerCase());
  }), [data, q]);

  const onRefresh = useCallback(() => {
    setRefreshing(true);
    setTimeout(() => setRefreshing(false), 1000);
  }, []);

  return (
    <FlatList
      data={filtered}
      keyExtractor={item => item.id}
      renderItem={({item}) => <ContactRow c={item} />}
      refreshControl={<RefreshControl refreshing={refreshing} onRefresh={onRefresh} />}
    />
  );
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this for thousands of items with virtualization and memory constraints?
- How would you add accessibility labels for screen readers?
- What metrics would you collect to verify rendering performance after changes?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to build a basic, performative list in RN with local data, search, skeleton loading, and rendering optimizations. Also checks understanding of stable item keys and accessibility.

## Key Concepts
- FlatList virtualization
- useMemo and React.memo
- keyExtractor and getItemLayout
- basic accessibility

## Code Example
```javascript
import React, { useMemo, useState, useCallback } from 'react';
import { FlatList, TextInput, View, Text } from 'react-native';

const Item = React.memo(({ name }) => <Text accessibilityLabel={`item-${name}`}>{name}</Text>);

export default function ItemList({ data }) {
  const [q, setQ] = useState('');
  const filtered = useMemo(() => data.filter(i => i.name.toLowerCase().includes(q.toLowerCase())), [data, q]);
  const renderItem = useCallback(({ item }) => <Item name={item.name} />, []);
  return (
    <View>
      <TextInput value={q} onChangeText={setQ} placeholder="Search" accessibilityLabel="search" />
      <FlatList
        data={filtered}
        keyExtractor={item => item.id}
        renderItem={renderItem}
        getItemLayout={(_, index) => ({ length: 48, offset: 48 * index, index })}
        initialNumToRender={20}
      />
    </View>
  );
}
```

